com/bb_api.h,com/ioctl_tab.c: add BB_GET/SET_RETX_EVENT_STATUS, missing from this SDK build entirely

The AR8030 baseband implements a windowed retransmission controller
(busy/idle/consecutive-window thresholds deciding when the link is
declared "in trouble" enough to lean harder on retx/hop/power-adjust)
that this SDK build's own header/dispatch table never learned about --
same class of host-side-only gap as 0028's own BB_SET_MCS_ITEM fix
(BB_REQ_GET jumps 16->100, BB_REQ_SET jumps 36->50, both opcodes sit in
the gap).

Unlike 0028, the opcode/struct here were first identified by an
external static-analysis writeup of the AR8030 baseband firmware and
vendor streamer binary (bb_demo_sky_3v3.img / ar_ldyhs_sky), not this
project's own decompile -- but this project independently confirmed
both opcodes and the struct's size via Ghidra:

- BB_GET_RETX_EVENT_STATUS (0x01000014): ar_ldyhs_sky's own
  fpv_bb_debug_info_dump @ 0x0006a608 calls
  `bb_ioctl(dev, 0x01000014, 0, &out)` immediately before printing
  out's first 5 bytes as "win=%d,busy=%d,idle=%d,conti busy=%d,conti
  idle=%d". Raw bytes at the opcode literal's own address (0x0006a62c)
  read `14 00 00 01` little-endian = 0x01000014, confirming
  BB_REQUEST(BB_REQ_GET, 20).
- BB_SET_RETX_EVENT_STATUS (0x02000026): ar_ldyhs_sky's own
  fpv_bb_init @ 0x000687e8 does `memset(&cfg, 0, 0x88)` (136 bytes),
  writes win/busy/idle/conti_busy/conti_idle at byte offsets 0-4 (from
  vendor defaults 10,{6,4,2,0} or a config struct when set), then
  `bb_ioctl(dev, 0x02000026, &cfg, 0)`. Raw bytes at that opcode
  literal's own address (0x00068d5c) read `26 00 00 02` little-endian
  = 0x02000026, confirming BB_REQUEST(BB_REQ_SET, 38). No other xref
  to this opcode was found in ar_ldyhs_sky -- it is only ever called
  once, at init, so whether a live SET after boot takes effect is
  still unverified on real hardware.

Only the first 5 of the struct's 136 bytes are recovered from either
call site (fpv_bb_debug_info_dump's own destination buffer for the GET
call is itself only 8 bytes, confirming the stock app never reads
further either); the remaining 131 bytes are kept as `reserved`
(bb_retx_cfg_t) rather than guessed at, same reasoning as 0030's own
bb_quality_t fix.

com/ioctl_tab.c needs a matching cmdtab[] entry for each new opcode
(0028's own precedent) since the client library's own
get_bb_ioctl_cmdiptlen()/get_bb_ioctl_cmdoutlen() reject any request
missing from that table before it ever reaches the daemon. No change
to com/ioctl_tab.c's daemon-side counterpart is needed: daemon/
normal_node.c's own client<->chip forwarding is a generic
reqid+payload passthrough with no ioctl_tab.c involvement, so the
unmodified stock RTOS firmware already understands both requests.

Mirrors sbc-groundstations' own identical patch.

--- a/com/bb_api.h
+++ b/com/bb_api.h
@@ -109,6 +109,27 @@
 #define BB_GET_RF                           BB_REQUEST(BB_REQ_GET, 15)  /**<@attention 获取RF状态*/
 #define BB_GET_SOCK_INFO                    BB_REQUEST(BB_REQ_GET, 16)  /**<@attention 获取系统socket的信息*/
 
+/**<@note Read the windowed retransmission controller's own event/status
+ * record: how aggressively the baseband declares this link "in trouble"
+ * and re-sends. NOT present in this SDK build's own header/dispatch
+ * table (order 20 -- the BB_REQ_GET numbering here jumps 16 -> 100 with
+ * nothing between), same class of host-side-only gap as BB_SET_MCS_ITEM
+ * above. Opcode independently confirmed by this project via Ghidra
+ * decompile of ar_ldyhs_sky's own fpv_bb_debug_info_dump @ 0x0006a608:
+ * `bb_ioctl(dev, 0x01000014, 0, &out)` immediately precedes printing
+ * out's first 5 bytes as "win=%d,busy=%d,idle=%d,conti busy=%d,conti
+ * idle=%d" (confirmed raw bytes at the opcode literal's own address,
+ * 0x0006a62c: 14 00 00 01 little-endian = 0x01000014) -- matches an
+ * external static-analysis writeup of the same firmware/binary that
+ * this was first sourced from. Notably, fpv_bb_debug_info_dump's own
+ * destination buffer for this call is only 8 bytes, confirming (not
+ * just asserting) that the stock app itself never reads past the first
+ * 5-6 bytes of the real reply either. See bb_retx_cfg_t's own comment
+ * for exactly what is and isn't verified (struct size and opcode: yes,
+ * independently confirmed twice over; live-SET-after-boot behavior and
+ * bytes 5-135's meaning: still no, needs real hardware). */
+#define BB_GET_RETX_EVENT_STATUS             BB_REQUEST(BB_REQ_GET, 20)
+
 #define BB_GET_REG                          BB_REQUEST(BB_REQ_GET, 100) /**<@note 基带寄存器读取命令字，本类型用于调试诊断*/
 #define BB_GET_CFG                          BB_REQUEST(BB_REQ_GET, 101) /**<@note 基带配置文件读取命令字*/
 #define BB_GET_DBG_MODE                     BB_REQUEST(BB_REQ_GET, 102) /**<@note 获取SDK debug模式状态*/
@@ -197,6 +218,56 @@
     uint16_t dw_keep_time;                                       /**<@note milliseconds*/
 } bb_set_mcs_item_t;
 
+/**<@note Set the windowed retransmission controller's own tuning
+ * parameters -- NOT the same mechanism as BB_SET_RETX_COUNT below (that
+ * one is a per-slot max-retries cap, bb_user_para_t.retx_count; this one
+ * is the busy/idle/consecutive-window thresholds that decide WHEN the
+ * baseband declares the link in enough trouble to lean on retx/hop/
+ * power-adjust harder -- distinct layers). NOT present in this SDK
+ * build's own header/dispatch table (order 38 -- jumps 36 -> 50 with
+ * nothing between), same host-side gap class as BB_SET_MCS_ITEM/
+ * BB_GET_RETX_EVENT_STATUS above. Opcode and struct size independently
+ * confirmed by this project via Ghidra decompile of ar_ldyhs_sky's own
+ * fpv_bb_init @ 0x000687e8: `memset(&cfg, 0, 0x88)` (136 bytes) then
+ * `cfg.win/busy/idle/conti_busy/conti_idle` written at byte offsets 0-4
+ * from vendor defaults (10, {6,4,2,0}) or gctx+0xc8/0xcc/0xd0/0xd4/0xd8
+ * when configured, then `bb_ioctl(dev, 0x02000026, &cfg, 0)` (confirmed
+ * raw bytes at the opcode literal's own address, 0x00068d5c: 26 00 00 02
+ * little-endian = 0x02000026). UNVERIFIED on real hardware whether a
+ * live SET after boot even takes effect -- the vendor app only ever
+ * calls this once, at its own init (confirmed by decompile: no other
+ * xref to this opcode found in ar_ldyhs_sky); see bb_retx_cfg_t's own
+ * comment before using this for anything beyond a read-back-after-write
+ * sanity check. */
+#define BB_SET_RETX_EVENT_STATUS             BB_REQUEST(BB_REQ_SET, 38)
+
+/**Define the windowed retransmission controller's shared config/status
+ * record (used by both BB_GET_RETX_EVENT_STATUS and
+ * BB_SET_RETX_EVENT_STATUS -- both opcodes independently confirmed by
+ * this project via Ghidra decompile, see their own comments above, to
+ * carry a matching 136-byte struct). Only the first 5 bytes are
+ * recovered (from the vendor app's own
+ * "win=%d,busy=%d,idle=%d,conti busy=%d,conti idle=%d" log format
+ * string, its GET-path print in fpv_bb_debug_info_dump, and its SET-path
+ * write in fpv_bb_init); the remaining 131 bytes are real record space
+ * of unknown layout, kept as `reserved` rather than guessed at -- same
+ * reasoning as this project's own bb_quality_t size fix (get the SIZE
+ * right first, decode fields once confirmed on hardware). Vendor
+ * defaults when unconfigured: win=10, {busy,idle,conti_busy,conti_idle}
+ * ={6,4,2,0}. UNVERIFIED: exact units of win/busy/idle/conti_busy/
+ * conti_idle (frames vs. windows), and whether a live SET after boot
+ * actually changes the running controller's behavior -- treat any
+ * control loop built on this as gated on confirming both first
+ * (ar8030-transport's own baseband-firmware-analysis Phase B). */
+typedef struct {
+    uint8_t win;         /**<@note retransmission window*/
+    uint8_t busy;         /**<@note windowed busy threshold*/
+    uint8_t idle;         /**<@note windowed idle threshold*/
+    uint8_t conti_busy;   /**<@note consecutive-busy threshold (name-inferred, not doc-confirmed)*/
+    uint8_t conti_idle;   /**<@note consecutive-idle threshold (name-inferred, not doc-confirmed)*/
+    uint8_t reserved[131]; /**<@note real record space, unknown layout -- see this struct's own comment above*/
+} bb_retx_cfg_t;
+
 #define BB_SET_RETX_COUNT                   BB_REQUEST(BB_REQ_SET, 50)  /**<@note 设置重传次数*/
 
 // 以下为调试诊断类命令字

